on fiber optic cable" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></div><div class="section-introduction xpfskxn"><h2 class="xhz5zt5">What this range covers</h2><p class="xuvmvsv">The connectorized side of a fiber build: patch cords for cross-connects and rack patching, adapters and cassette adapters for panels, MTP/MPO trunks and array cables for high-density data halls, terminal boxes for premises and tower sites, and hardened connectors for outdoor field termination. Each item is specified to your connector, polish, jacket rating and length.</p></div><div class="specification-table xcqzusx fb"><div class="construction-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Connector types</p><p class="xcclquv">LC, SC, FC, ST and MTRJ in UPC or APC polish, plus MTP/MPO</p></div><div class="strength-member-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Ratings</p><p class="xcclquv">OFNR riser, OFNP plenum and LSZH jackets, IP68 for outdoor boxes and connectors</p></div><div class="fibre-type-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Patch cords</p><p class="xcclquv">Simplex or duplex, 0.9mm pigtail or 2.0mm and 3.0mm jacket, UL listed</p></div><div class="fibre-counts-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">MTP/MPO assemblies</p><p class="xcclquv">Trunks 8F to 144F and array cables 8F to 32F, polarity A, B or C</p></div><div class="sheath-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Adapters</p><p class="xcclquv">SC, LC, FC, ST and MTRJ, zirconia ceramic sleeve, under 0.2dB insertion loss</p></div><div class="deployment-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Terminal boxes and field</p><p class="xcclquv">In-house boxes 1F to 4F, IP68 waterproof boxes 2F to 12F, OptiTap compatible connectors</p></div><div class="standards-row xr2tetp"><p class="xbslay4">Lead time</p><p class="xcclquv">6 to 8 weeks standard, 2 to 3 weeks by air, up to 10 weeks for custom builds</p></div></div></section><section class="fibre-count-range xqjs4fo"><h2 class="xqmzbdo">From one patch cord to a full data hall</h2><p class="xbt6gdt">A single cord for a cross-connect, or trunks and cassettes for a whole row. Specified per link and supplied to order.</p><div class="count-rail xhrktuh"><div class="144f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">1F</p></div><div class="288f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">2F</p></div><div class="432f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">8F</p></div><div class="576f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">12F</p></div><div class="864f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">24F</p></div><div class="1728f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">32F</p></div><div class="3456f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">144F</p></div></div></section><div class="section-divider xbstc8l"><div class="x2h0iev"></div><div class="xqo6eaw"></div><div class="x2h0iev"></div></div><div class="individual-products xjpxpkl"><h3 class="xntyyys">Browse connectors and hardware</h3><div class="product-links xawjyfv">{products.filter((item) => item.data.category === "Connectors, Terminal Boxes and Hardware").map((item) => (<ProductCard item={item} />))}</div></div><div class="section-divider xbstc8l"><div class="x2h0iev"></div><div class="xqo6eaw"></div><div class="x2h0iev"></div></div><section class="why-source-through-vocom x6mc4fb"><div class="why-introduction xn9jb0l"><h2 class="x2aydey">Why source connectors through Vocom</h2></div><div class="sourcing-reason-grid xyelmuz"><div class="build-to-order xwbyhvi fb"><svg class="xmhveue icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M 0 2.25 C 0 1.007 1.007 0 2.25 0 C 3.493 0 4.5 1.007 4.5 2.25 C 4.5 3.493 3.493 4.5 2.25 4.5 C 1.007 4.5 0 3.493 0 2.25 Z" fill-opacity="var(--icon-alpha, 0)" fill="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(7.5 5.25)"></path><path d="M 0 2.25 C 0 1.007 1.007 0 2.25 0 C 3.493 0 4.5 1.007 4.5 2.25 C 4.5 3.493 3.493 4.5 2.25 4.5 C 1.007 4.5 0 3.493 0 2.25 Z" fill-opacity="var(--icon-alpha, 0)" fill="var(--icon-color, rgb(0, 0, 0))" transform="translate(13.5 14.25)"></path><path d="M 0 2.25 C 0 1.007 1.007 0 2.25 0 C 3.493 0 4.5 1.007 4.5 2.25 C 4.5 3.493 3.493 4